From 2ba56d72941ffa20f50da5c05662a127b08a8c8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kunstbanause <3209654+Kunstbanause@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:23:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] d/rift_s: Replace the CV1 placeholder distortion with a
 Rift S lens model

The driver corrected the Rift S lenses with Rift CV1 values (74 mm lens
separation, 105 degree FOV, CV1 coefficients), which makes the image warp
and swim when turning the head and distorts depth at the view edges.

- Read the per-unit lens calibration from firmware block 0x12 (lens
  optical centres and eye-cup distances, in panel pixels).
- Use the per-eye FOV and centre pixel density reported by the Oculus
  runtime for the Rift S (hmdgdb OculusRiftS_Native_R80): left eye
  L/R/U/D 44/46/45/49 degrees, 823.28 px per tangent, mirrored for the
  right eye.
- Map panel pixels to tangent angles around the lens centre with a
  radial term tan = s (1 + c1 s^2 + c2 s^4); c1 = 0.47 fitted to the
  eye-cup distances at the FOV edges. RIFT_S_DISTORTION_C1/_C2 tune it,
  RIFT_S_DISTORTION=cv1 restores the old placeholder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
